**Replay audit.** The input schema maxima are **19 / 32**. Dash uses logical bit **18**, wire bit **31**. The one-line 48-bit mask change preserves bits 31 and 32 through packing, unpacking and JSON. `ReplayLog` and `InputTape` retain the packed integer. `ControlsReplay`, `LiveInput` and `PlayerActions` needed no edits. One remaining 32-bit field matters to the ghost lane: `stage_pilot.gd:134` writes `_previous` with `put_32`, so its digest includes dash bit 31 and omits ghost bit 32. Live edge detection retains both.

**Verification.** Quick gates and commit hooks passed. The changed-unit run had **3,789 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped**. All **67 scenarios passed**, including shipped replays and the two-bake golden comparison. After the cooldown correction, **20 focused tests passed** and native parity matched over **1,200 steps**. Mutation score was **15/20 (75%)**, with five survivors and zero timeouts. Godot emitted resource-cleanup warnings after the successful scenario run. I stopped duplicate full-unit and standalone bake runs before the hard stop. The full scenario result predates the cooldown correction.

